SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Latinas Leading Business
LOCATION:Scotties
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 84 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 03636\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nIn celebration of Hispan
 ic Heritage Month\, join us for a ’Quin Chat that shines a light on the 
 growing influence of Latinas shaping America’s economic future. Drawing
  from a new national study focused on U.S. Latinas\, the conversation wi
 ll explore their expanding  economic power\, leadership\, and impact—an
 d why this generation of leaders represents a force poised to shape the f
 uture of business and the broader U.S. economy.\n\nThe research began in 2
 025\, when the Latino Donor Collaborative\, Hispanics in Philanthropy\, an
 d We Are ALX - grant recipient of The 'Quin Impact Fund - a joined forces 
 to envision a national study capturing the economic contributions and pote
 ntial of U.S. Latinas. Moderated by Nathalie Rayes\, former U.S. Ambassado
 r to Croatia and civic leader\, the conversation brings together three of 
 the original thought partners behind the study: Eneida Roman\, President a
 nd CEO of We Are ALX and a nationally recognized advocate for advancing wo
 men and Latinos\; Ana Marie Argilagos\, former President & CEO of Hispanic
 s in Philanthropy\; and Ana Valdez\, President & CEO of the Latino Donor C
 ollaborative. Together\, they will share the story behind the research\, a
 nd consider what the rising influence of Latinas means for business\, lead
 ership\, and philanthropy.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members plus 3 registered guests. Complimentary light bites and refresh
 ments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at leas
 t 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203636
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-205637@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261006T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T133000
SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation: The Future of Medicine
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/205637\n\n12:00PM  - 1:30
 PM Program\nWhat will it take to accelerate the next generation of medical
  breakthroughs—and rethink how discoveries make their way from the lab t
 o the people who need them? In the latest edition of 90 Minutes of Innovat
 ion\, John Werner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI colu
 mnist\, and Alexander Wissner-Gross\, research scientist and entrepreneur\
 , sit down with Peter Kolchinsky\, PhD\, Founder and Managing Partner of R
 A Capital Management and author of The Great American Drug Deal\, for a co
 nversation at the intersection of science\, technology\, investment\, and 
 healthcare.\n\nWith a PhD in Virology from Harvard University\, Kolchinsky
  has spent decades investing in companies developing drugs\, medical devic
 es\, diagnostics\, and research tools\, while advocating for approaches th
 at make medicines more affordable without sacrificing the innovation behin
 d tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Through his work with RA Capital and No Pati
 ent Left Behind\, he has become a leading voice in conversations surroundi
 ng biotechnology\, drug development\, affordability\, and the incentives t
 hat shape the future of medicine.\n\nTogether\, Werner\, Wissner-Gross\, a
 nd Kolchinsky will explore how artificial intelligence and emerging techno
 logies could accelerate scientific discovery\, reshape the development of 
 new treatments\, and transform the broader healthcare landscape. From gett
 ing promising discoveries to patients faster to balancing affordability wi
 th continued investment in innovation\, expect a wide-ranging conversation
  about what’s possible when science\, technology\, and new ways of think
 ing converge.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly as
 k that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of t
 he event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/205637
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-207308@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261006T140000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Unlocking Longevity at WHOOP
LOCATION:Offsite - WHOOP Headquarters
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 4 spots left
 \nStatus: Available\nTime: 2 PM – 6 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequ
 inhouse.com/events/207308\n\nWhat does it mean to live not only longer\, b
 ut better? Join us at WHOOP Headquarters in Kenmore Square where a select 
 number of seats have been reserved exclusively for ‘Quin members at TEDx
 Boston: Unlocking Longevity. Bringing together leading voices across scien
 ce\, medicine\, technology\, and biotechnology\, the afternoon will explor
 e the research\, ideas\, and innovations shaping the future of human healt
 h and longevity.\n\nAcross seventeen short-form talks presented in three b
 locks\, experts will explore the research and innovation shaping the futur
 e of longevity\, spanning epigenetic reprogramming\, GLP-1s and metabolic 
 health\, immune aging\, women’s longevity\, artificial intelligence\, an
 d the continuous data transforming prevention into daily practice. The thr
 oughline: rigor over hype\, and research with the potential to reach the c
 linic.\n\nFeatured speakers include Peter Kolchinsky\, Managing Partner of
  RA Capital Management and founder of No Patient Left Behind\; Andrew Brac
 k\, Program Manager at ARPA-H\; Dr. Saranya Wyles\, Medical Director at Ma
 yo Clinic\; Alexandra Drane of ARCHANGELS\; J. Sawalla Guseh of Mass Gener
 al Brigham\; Kayla Barnes-Lentz of Ammortal\; Alexander (AJ) Blood of AIwi
 thCare\; and more.\n\nSpend the afternoon at the forefront of the longevit
 y conversation\, with a closer look at the research\, technologies\, and i
 deas that could shape not simply how long we live\, but how well.\n\n*This
  event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Please be aware tha
 t members attending this event will need to sign a WHOOP NDA at arrival. 
 We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to th
 e start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/207308
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
