SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Decoding Gut Health
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only
 \nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/205638\n\n5:30PM Rece
 ption\, 6:00PM Discussion \nIn an oversaturated health and wellness lands
 cape shaped by trends\, social media\, and an ever-growing marketplace\, h
 ow do we separate fact from fiction when it comes to gut health? Join us f
 or a ’Quin Chat exploring the science of the gut microbiome and its conn
 ection to digestion\, immunity\, metabolism\, and overall well-being. Toge
 ther\, our panelists will unpack what the research really tells us about p
 robiotics\, prebiotics\, fermented foods\, fiber\, microbiome testing\, an
 d personalized nutrition.\n\nThe conversation brings together leading voic
 es at the intersection of medicine\, microbiome research\, and emerging te
 chnology: Dr. Lynne B. Ahn\, MD\, gastroenterologist and Founder and Medic
 al Director of Ahn Point Wellness\; John Capodilupo\, Co-Founder and forme
 r CTO of WHOOP and Co-Founder and CPO of Throne\; Dr. Brantley Hall\, PhD\
 , Co-Founder of Ventoscity\; and Dr. Chethan Ramprasad\, MS\, MS\, gastroe
 nterologist at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center and faculty member at 
 Harvard Medical School. From AI and wearable technology to digital biomark
 ers and new approaches to monitoring digestive health\, they will explore 
 what’s proven\, what is promising\, and what the future of gut health ma
 y hold.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Com
 plimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.We kindly ask that 
 all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the even
 t.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/205638
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206195@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261007T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Communities Changing Healthcare
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 31 spot
 s left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/eve
 nts/206195\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\n\nWhat if some of the 
 most consequential ideas in American healthcare are not coming out of rese
 arch labs or Silicon Valley—but from the communities that have been quie
 tly reimagining access to care for decades?\n\nJoin us for a timely conver
 sation exploring the evolution of community health centers: how a movement
  born from the pursuit of more equitable\, community-driven care became an
  essential part of the healthcare landscape—and what its next chapter co
 uld look like.\n\nDr. Michael Curry\, Esq.\, President & CEO of the Massac
 husetts League of Community Health Centers\, will be joined by Dr. Thomas 
 Ward\, historian\, Dean of the School of Arts and Sciences at Farmingdale 
 State College\, and author of Out in the Rural\, and Dr. James Hunt\, Jr.\
 , former CEO of the Massachusetts League and author of If You’ve Seen On
 e\, a new book chronicling the health center movement.\n\nTogether\, the p
 anel will look beyond the traditional healthcare model to explore how comm
 unity health centers have evolved around the people they serve\, the force
 s reshaping their work today\, and what decades of community-based care ca
 n teach us about building a healthier\, more equitable future.\n\n*This ev
 ent is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bi
 tes and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations 
 be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206195
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
