SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Safekeeping" by Claudia Hinz
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203629
 \n\nThis October\, settle into the season with Safekeeping by Claudia Hinz
 \, a sweeping and deeply moving novel about family\, memory\, and the secr
 ets we carry across generations. Set against the rugged beauty of Northern
  California\, the story follows the intertwined lives of three women as lo
 ng-held truths begin to surface\, revealing the complicated bonds between 
 mothers and daughters and the choices that shape a family over time.\n\nAt
 mospheric and richly layered\, Safekeeping explores belonging\, resilience
 \, and the ways our past continues to shape the present. With its evocativ
 e setting and intimate exploration of family relationships\, it is a fitti
 ng fall read—and an ideal choice for readers drawn to thoughtful\, chara
 cter-driven stories that linger long after the final page.\n\nJoined by au
 thor Claudia Hinz\, the evening will offer a closer look at the inspiratio
 n behind Safekeeping\, its characters\, and the themes woven throughout th
 e novel. Members will have the opportunity to hear directly from Hinz and 
 explore the story through an intimate conversation that brings the book - 
 and the world within it - to life.\n\n*This event is complimentary and res
 erved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be
  served.We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours pri
 or to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203629
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206905@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261013T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T203000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Modern Parenting - Navigating Teen Mental Health Togeth
 er
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 110 spo
 ts left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/e
 vents/206905\n\n7:00PM Reception\, 7:30PM Discussion\n\nWhat is simply par
 t of being a teenager—and when does it warrant a closer look? Join us fo
 r an expert-led ’Quin Chat exploring the mental health and well-being of
  today’s teenagers and how parents can better understand and support the
 m through these formative years. At a time marked by significant physical\
 , emotional\, and social change - and amplified by social media\, constant
  connectivity\, academic pressures\, and an increasingly digital world - o
 ur panel will explore what constitutes typical teenage behavior\, signs th
 at may warrant greater attention\, and how parents can approach difficult 
 conversations and offer meaningful support.\n\nModerated by Kimberlyn Lear
 y\, PhD\, MPA\, associate professor of psychology at the Harvard Medical S
 chool and Senior Advisor at McLean Hospital\, the conversation will bring 
 together adolescent mental health and pediatric experts Cecil Webster\, MD
 \, psychiatrist\, psychoanalyst\, and CEO of Webster Clinic\; Jacqueline B
 uchanan\, MD\, psychiatrist at Webster Clinic\; and Essential Pediatrics C
 o-Founders Brenda Anders Pring\, MD\, and Christina Nordt\, MD. Together\,
  they will offer expert perspective on changing moods\, growing independen
 ce\, anxiety\, social pressures\, technology\, and the evolving parent-tee
 n relationship—with practical guidance for helping teenagers navigate it
  all.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compl
 imentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that a
 ll cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206905
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206907@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: From Head Of The Charles to Los Angeles 2028 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: Sports & Games\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 150 spots 
 left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/206907\n\n5:00PM Discussion\, 5:30PM Reception\n\nAs the rowing world t
 urns its attention to Boston for one of the sport’s most celebrated week
 ends\, join us for a timely ’Quin Chat with NBC10 Boston Host Hannah Don
 nelly and two-time Olympic rower and Massachusetts native\, Kristi Wagner.
  Fresh off competing at the World Rowing Championships\, Wagner will share
  an inside look at her experience on the international stage\, the trainin
 g and determination required to compete among the world’s best\, and wha
 t comes next as she sets her sights on earning another Olympic berth for t
 he Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Donnelly and Wagner will 
 dive into the excitement surrounding this year’s Head Of The Charles Reg
 atta\, where Wagner will once again take to the water\, and explore what m
 akes the iconic race such a defining moment for Boston and the global rowi
 ng community. Their conversation will also take a broader look at the stat
 e of U.S. women’s rowing\, the athletes and momentum shaping its future\
 , and the road ahead as the sport builds toward Los Angeles in 2028. From 
 racing on the Charles to competing on the world’s biggest stage\, the ev
 ening offers a rare glimpse into the life of an elite athlete and the ambi
 tion\, preparation\, and perseverance behind the pursuit of Olympic excell
 ence.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compl
 imentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that a
 ll cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206907
CATEGORIES:Sports & Games
END:VEVENT
