BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206906@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T193000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Starting Over with John and Yoko" with Roger Farringt
 on and Kenneth Womack
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 110 spots left\n
 Status: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206
 906\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\n\nFresh off the book’s laun
 ch in New York City\, join us for Boston’s exclusive first look at “St
 arting Over with John and Yoko”\, featuring Boston-based photographer Ro
 ger Farrington and renowned Beatles historian and author Kenneth Womack. T
 he book transports readers back to August 7th\, 1980\, when John Lennon an
 d Yoko Ono returned to the recording studio after a five-year absence to b
 egin work on what would become “Double Fantasy”. Farrington\, then an 
 up-and-coming photographer\, was given the assignment of a lifetime: captu
 re the image that would announce Lennon’s return to music. Just four mon
 ths later\, Lennon’s assassination would transform those photographs int
 o a poignant record of one of music history’s final chapters.\n\nIn conv
 ersation\, Farrington and Womack will take members inside Manhattan’s Hi
 t Factory and behind the images from that extraordinary day\, sharing the 
 stories and circumstances surrounding a moment few could have known would 
 become so significant. Featuring the complete collection of Farrington’s
  photographs from the session for the first time\, “Starting Over with J
 ohn and Yoko” also offers a fascinating glimpse into celebrity photograp
 hy in the pre-digital era. Drawing on Farrington’s decades photographing
  some of the world’s most recognizable figures and Womack’s extensive 
 scholarship on the Beatles and John Lennon\, the conversation will explore
  photography\, music\, memory\, and the enduring cultural legacy of Lennon
  and Ono.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. C
 omplimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask th
 at all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the e
 vent.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206906
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
